.TH PWMIX 1 "October 2026" "pwmix 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pwmix \- mixer-style view for PipeWire
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pwmix
[\fB\-\-png\fR \fIFILE\fR [\fB\-\-size\fR \fIWIDTH HEIGHT\fR]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows PipeWire applications, devices and the links between them as
columns of mixer strips with volume and mute controls. Application
streams are matched to the desktop window that owns them.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-png " FILE"
Render one frame of the current graph to a PNG file and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-size " WIDTH HEIGHT"
Window or image size in pixels.
.SH CONTROLS
Mouse wheel over a strip changes its volume. Clicking the M button
toggles mute. Up, Down, Page Up and Page Down scroll. Q or Escape quits.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Requires an X11 session (DISPLAY) and a running PipeWire daemon.
.SH AUTHOR
NetLinux <graham@netlinux.co.uk>
